\f0\fs28 \cf0 File Storage and Naming Conventions for Anomaloscope Data\
(Notes by Deena Elul 6/28/19)\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9642 
\f0 	}After testing, anomaloscope data files should be printed as .xps documents and saved on a USB drive. The files can then be moved to MTRP_data/Exp_Anomaloscope\
{\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9642 
\f0 	}Each subject\'92s data are stored in an individual folder (folder name = subject ID) \
{\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9642 
\f0 	}File naming convention: SubjectID_test number \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Ex: MELA_3xxx_1\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	
\f1 \uc0\u9642 
\f0 	}Each subject should have four data files corresponding to four anomaloscope specific tests:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}deuteranopia (1)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}protanopia (2)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}deuteranopia (3)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}protanopia (4)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
